1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,360
Google wants to invest 15 billion USD in Malaysia.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,880
That's good.

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:07,700
But are there jobs for our people?

4
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:18,080
Because a data centre isn't just a building full of computers.

5
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,400
Building it, maintaining it, managing it —

6
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:22,420
all of it needs a workforce.

7
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,980
Engineers, technicians, contractors, logistics people.

8
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,640
Google expects this latest investment

9
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:32,540
to support more than 37,000 jobs a year during construction.

10
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:36,820
Once operational, more than 9,000 jobs a year.

11
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,940
These are jobs created by Google's ecosystem —

12
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,000
not all of them with Google itself.

13
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,760
For me, the measure of success

14
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,280
isn't how many billions in investment are announced,

15
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:50,820
but how many Malaysians get good jobs,

16
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:53,700
and how many local companies get opportunities.

17
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,340
That is what we must make sure of.
